{#
    The tax-province explanatory paragraph, shared by PurchaseOrder's and VendorBill's VIEW screens
    (`purchase_order_detail.html.twig`'s `#po-delivery-province` and `bill_detail.html.twig`'s
    `#bill-receiving-warehouse`). The caller keeps its own wrapping `<div id="...">` — this partial
    renders only the branching text inside it.

    The two screens' current wording is NOT identical even for the shared cases — PurchaseOrder
    states "an order with taxable goods and no province cannot be issued" only inside the Draft
    remedy block, while VendorBill states its equivalent unconditionally, right after the headline.
    That is an existing, real difference between what each screen currently says, not a fact this
    partial invents an opinion about: `cannotFreezeHere` / `cannotFreezeInDraftBlock` let each
    caller keep placing its own sentence exactly where it already did. Forcing the two placements to
    match would be a wording change dressed up as a template one, and several Cests
    (`PurchaseOrderProvinceSentenceReEvaluatesCest`, `BillEditProvinceSentenceReEvaluatesCest` and
    their `WarehouseAddressDerives*` siblings) assert on the exact current copy.

    VendorBill's own Disputed-status remedy ("Return this bill to draft...") is NOT part of this
    partial — PurchaseOrder has no Disputed status, so `bill_detail.html.twig` appends it itself,
    directly after including this partial, as the one real exception this move keeps separate.

    Parameters
    ----------
    documentNoun              required  'order' | 'bill'
    hasProvince               required  Whether the document carries a frozen province.
    provinceDisplay            optional  The frozen value's display text (both screens show the
                                        bare code). Only read when `hasProvince`.
    provinceTail                optional  The rest of the "Tax province: X, ..." sentence — see the
                                        docblock note above on why the two screens' wording differs
                                        here. Only read when `hasProvince`.
    warehouse                  optional  The document's warehouse (PurchaseOrder's is effectively
                                        always set; VendorBill's can be null).
    showWarehouseClause        optional  Whether to append a "— warehouse has no province" clause
                                        to the "No tax province recorded" headline. Default false.
    warehouseClauseText         optional  That clause's text — PurchaseOrder names the warehouse,
                                        VendorBill's current copy does not (an existing difference,
                                        not one this move introduces).
    cannotFreezeSentence         optional  "An order with taxable goods and no province cannot be
                                        issued." / "A bill with taxable goods and no province cannot
                                        be approved."
    cannotFreezeHere            optional  Print `cannotFreezeSentence` right after the headline
                                        (VendorBill's placement). Default false.
    cannotFreezeInDraftBlock    optional  Print it at the end of the Draft remedy block instead
                                        (PurchaseOrder's placement). Default false.
    showDraftRemedy             optional  Whether to show the "now records" / "record the address"
                                        remedy block — each caller folds its own extra guard (a
                                        warehouse actually being named, for VendorBill) into this
                                        one boolean rather than the partial re-deriving it.
#}
{% set warehouse = warehouse|default(null) %}
{% if hasProvince %}
    Tax province <strong>{{ provinceDisplay|default('') }}</strong>, {{ provinceTail|default('') }}
{% else %}
    <strong>No tax province recorded on this {{ documentNoun }}</strong>{% if showWarehouseClause|default(false) %} — {{ warehouseClauseText|default('') }}{% endif %}, so nothing here computed provincial tax.
    {% if cannotFreezeHere|default(false) %} {{ cannotFreezeSentence|default('') }}{% endif %}
    {% if showDraftRemedy|default(false) %}
        {% if warehouse and warehouse.province %}
            <strong>{{ warehouse.name }} now records {{ warehouse.province }}</strong> — this {{ documentNoun }} was entered before that, and the province is taken from the warehouse each time the draft is saved. Save this draft again to freeze it onto the {{ documentNoun }}.
        {% else %}
            Record the address under Config &rsaquo; Warehouses, then save this draft again.
        {% endif %}
        {% if cannotFreezeInDraftBlock|default(false) %} {{ cannotFreezeSentence|default('') }}{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
